{"kind":"rule","id":"sched","title":"Scheduler timeout","type":"timer","context":"p-net main thread (pnet_handle_periodic)","notes":"`pf_scheduler_restart` removes a running timeout and calls `pf_scheduler_add` with its own `cb` parameter, which is why one site inside it has an unresolved handler.","send":[{"call":"pf_scheduler_add","handler":3},{"call":"pf_scheduler_restart","handler":3}]}
{"kind":"rule","id":"app-cb","title":"Application callback","type":"callback","notes":"The stack calls the application through `net->fspm_cfg.<name>_cb`. This repository contains no application, so the only registrations found are in the integration test fixture (`test/utils_for_testing.cpp`); they are left unconfirmed on purpose.","send":[{"invoke":".*_cb"}],"receive":[{"assign":".*_cb","as":"handler"}]}
{"kind":"rule","id":"bg","title":"Background worker event","type":"event","context":"background worker thread","notes":"`pf_bg_worker_start_job` sets one event bit per job; `bg_worker_task` waits on the event and tests each bit.","send":[{"call":"os_event_set","key":2}],"receive":[{"test":"BG_JOB_EVENT_.*"}]}
